-- Combine rule (same as steal): empty dropdown = ignored; any set dropdown is a
-- filter; multiple set = AND. A pet must match every non-empty filter to sell.
--
-- The current GUI.SellPrompt uses PetSatchel.SellSelection with explicit
-- Assets/Eggs UID arrays, without equipping a Tool. Keep filtered sales bounded
-- to the freshly verified UID selection and confirm its removal. The
-- legacy SellEveryPet path is never used (it ignored filtered IDs in Sept 2 tests).
--
-- Sellable set (mirrors the NPC's own filter exactly):
--   `Save.Get().Inventory` (deserialized via Util.AssetItemSerialization)
--   minus IsFavorite, minus `Save.Get().EquippedAssets`, minus InFuse.
-- ⚠️ That is a DIFFERENT set from `GetOwnerRuntimeRecords` (= your 15 equipped
-- pets) which the old filters wrongly listed — equipped pets can't be sold at all.
-- Favorite a pet in-game to hard-protect it from every sell path here.
SellBox = SellTab:AddLeftGroupbox("💰 Sell Pets")

-- Auto-Place has a similarly named helper inside its own register-saving scope.
-- Keep the seller copy local to this HOME/SELL scope so Luau does not resolve an
-- out-of-scope call as a nil global when either Auto-Sell toggle is armed.
local function sellFilterHasChoice(store)
    for _, enabled in pairs(store or {}) do
        if enabled == true then return true end
    end
    return false
end

